[1749.971273, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;160m\u001b[48;5;224m    -\u001b[38;5;236mrandomized trials. We also report that the unweighted pCR rates were almost identical ({{pcr_crude_du\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;160m\u001b[48;5;224m    -\u001b[38;5;236mal}} and {{pcr_crude_single}}) and explain why, and we show that the data were insufficient to assess\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;160m\u001b[48;5;224m    -\u001b[38;5;236m event-free or overall survival. We believe that this transparent handling of treatment-era confoundi\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;160m\u001b[48;5;224m    -\u001b[38;5;236mng in a regional real-world cohort will interest the readers of the Journal, many of whom face the sa\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;160m    -\u001b[38;5;236mme question when interpreting their own institutional data.                                          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;29m\u001b[48;5;194m 11 +\u001b[38;5;236mDual HER2 blockade was associated with a higher pCR rate (odds ratio, {{pcr_or|b}}), consistent with \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;29m    +\u001b[38;5;236mrandomized trials. We also report that the unweighted pCR rates were al"]
[1749.971522, "o", "most identical\u001b[48;5;157m,\u001b[48;5;194m \u001b[48;5;157mat \u001b[48;5;194m{{pcr_crude\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;29m\u001b[48;5;194m    +\u001b[38;5;236m_dual}} and {{pcr_crude_single}}\u001b[48;5;157m,\u001b[48;5;194m and explain why, and we show that the data were insufficient to ass\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;29m\u001b[48;5;194m    +\u001b[38;5;236mess event-free or overall survival. We believe that this transparent handling of treatment-era confou\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;29m    +\u001b[38;5;236mnding in a regional real-world cohort will interest the readers of the Journal, many of whom face the\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;29m\u001b[48;5;194m    +\u001b[38;5;236m same question when interpreting their own institutional data.                                       \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;236m\u001b[2m 12 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;236m\u001b[2m 13 \u001b[22m We confirm that this manuscript has not been published, is not under consideration for publication el\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;236m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m sewhere, and has not been presented at a scientific meeting, and that there are no r"]
